  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to the Bohr&#39;s atomic theory, the kinetic energy of an electron is directly proportional to the square of the atomic number and inversely proportional to the square of the principal quantum number.&nbsp;</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KE</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mfrac><mi>eV</mi><mi>atom</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>KE&#945;</mi><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>(B) speed of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>n&#945;z</mi></math></p><p>(C)&nbsp;Frequency of revolution of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>(D)&nbsp;Coulombic force of attraction on the electron is directly proportional to the square of the atomic number and inversely proportional to the fourth power of the principal quantum number.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>kq</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>kze</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>r&#945;</mi><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F&#945;</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>F&#945;</mi><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p>"
